From 0d0ee3a326d8666efdda877524e9ef3f7c6bddee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:49:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(api): report per-provider-request context usage beside
 turn billing totals [daveey]

Chat Completions usage.prompt_tokens is the sum of every provider call in a
gateway turn (billing). Consumers (BB-1207) read it as one request's context
size, so a two-call turn looked like a 2x context peak.

Add optional usage.context_usage = {version:1, complete, requests:[{provider,
model, input_tokens, input_limit|null}]}: one entry per main-loop provider
response, captured once before MoA fold under the identity that served it,
reset per run_conversation, capped at 128. complete=false when any response
could not be measured individually (no usage, diverted, adapter-aggregated:
MoA advisors, codex app-server, hosted tools, multi-hop decode). input_limit is
the resolved runtime window minus output reservation; null when guessed or for
another runtime. Billing totals, routing and limits are unchanged. Emitted on
streaming and non-streaming chat completions, direct and canonical paths.
